{:id "0012-rules-hardening"
 :title "Rules: validate presence documents and the inside of messages"
 :lupa/deps #{"0009-rules"}
 :lupa/area :security
 :lupa/risk :high
 :goal "A member can only write well-formed data, even into documents they
        own. Today a member may write any shape into their own presence
        document, and a message's emphasis items and inReplyTo are not
        type-checked."
 :scope ["firestore.rules" "test-rules/halfahead/rules_test.clj"]
 :design "In firestore.rules:
          - presence write: keys().hasOnly and hasAll ['memberId',
            'conversationId', 'state', 'since']; memberId == the path's
            memberId; conversationId == cid; state in ['idle', 'thinking'];
            since == request.time. Presence may be created and updated, not
            deleted.
          - message create additionally: inReplyTo, when present, is a
            string of size 1..128; every emphasis item is a map with exactly
            integer 'from' and 'to', 0 <= from < to <= text.size(). Rules
            have no loops: check items 0..7 with a helper that is true for
            an index past the list's end.
          Keep every existing allowed and denied case passing."
 :acceptance
 ["Allowed: own presence with the right shape and request.time; a message
   with two valid emphasis spans and a string inReplyTo"
  "Denied: presence with an extra key, a wrong memberId field, state
   \"away\", or a client-chosen since; presence delete; a message with an
   emphasis item missing 'to', with from >= to, with to past the text's end,
   or with a non-integer; a message whose inReplyTo is a number"
  "All existing rules tests still pass; `bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit bb.edn, the emulator runner, or any src/ file"
  "No changes to who may read what"]
 :context ["firestore.rules" "test-rules/halfahead/rules_test.clj"
           "docs/SCHEMA.md" "src/halfahead/codec.cljc"]
 :budget-usd 8.0}
